sing and they want us to make this  decision as soon as we possibly can so  that they have the security of knowing  how their benefits will be next year I  get that completely but I can't possibly  make the decision and on my own now we  need to get the figures get everything  at our disposal and then I will make  sure that we make that decision as  quickly as possible okay but it's going  to cost 5 billion pounds if you go with  inflation how will you pay for that I  think um the difference between between  the two figures wages or inflation is  about half of that in fact  um so but obviously it depends on what  those figures are but we'll know a lot  more next week is really important that  we make sure that we target the  government resources at the most  vulnerable this winter  um okay talk to me about the SMP if you  would it's their conference at the  moment in Aberdeen and Nicola sturgeon  says she detests everything the Tories  stand for how do you feel about her well  I don't think that's great language to  use and actually frankly when you look  at the global situation we're in and the  war that we were just talking about I  really think it's quite important that  we're able politely to disagree with  each other in this country we are so  fortunate we can have a democratic  system so much that we take for granted  and we ought to be able to have sensible  discussion about policy without  detesting each other there's no need  okay politics of the playground well I  it's just not how we do things I don't  think  um talk to me about some suggestions in  the newspapers this morning that I'm  reading that Tom Watson should be given  a period that was knocked back a couple  of years ago but sakiristama is looking  again at uh Tom Watson getting a period  what do you think well it's a matter for  the labor party who they put forward for  parentages  well I've never really I I'm I'm not the  world expert on that story I know that  there was there was well let me tell you  yeah yeah yeah he he um had been accused  um or he his he has now been Consulting  the victims of false sex abuse  allegations  um lady Britain as in um yeah his widow  branded Mr Watson despicable and  defensive as you know he was falsely  accused of rape and child abuse as a  result of this uh campaign that had been  conducted at the time  um Harvey Proctor falsely accused of  being a child murderer by this fantasist  as well supported by um Tom Watson  should he get a peerage well the my  difficulty is Kate is that I I don't  know what Tom Watson believed I don't  know I I'm really can't advocate for him  in any way he was clearly taken in by  somebody who was making up very  unpleasant and and malicious stories  about prominent men at the time what Tom  Watson believed at any one time I really  can't so you wouldn't it wasn't  something that you would say well I  think it's very important that anybody  who gets a period should be very  carefully investigated and I do think to  go to your earlier point that it is  quite important that we're very careful  in public life about who we accuse of  what yeah um so everybody should be  thoroughly investigated before they get  a period what about Conor Burns  I don't think there's any suggestion  that Conor Burns is getting a period  yeah there is yeah yeah there is  um yeah apparently um his name is on the  list that um the former prime minister  has put forward uh well I haven't heard  that what do you think should he get one  um I think where we are what's happened  I I don't know any more about that well  I probably know less about the facts of  the incident than you do I think what's  important is that the chief whip has  been asked to investigate this I think  that she must do that as quickly and as  thoroughly as possible it's a really  difficult situation for all involved not  least  um the the accuser the the victim the  alleged victim if you like and I think  it's really important that we we solve  um 